   "source": [
    "# ECG Arrhythmia Classification — VMD, beat alignment, and a chirplet comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "`ECGData.mat`: 162 records x 65536 samples, **fs = 128 Hz** (512 s per record).\n",
    "\n",
    "| Class | Records | Source |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| ARR | 96 | MIT-BIH Arrhythmia |\n",
    "| CHF | 30 | BIDMC Congestive Heart Failure |\n",
    "| NSR | 36 | MIT-BIH Normal Sinus Rhythm |\n",
    "\n",
    "Every number below is **subject-held-out** (`StratifiedGroupKFold` on record ID).\n",
    "Headline result:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Configuration | Accuracy | Macro-F1 |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Baseline, no decomposition | 0.686 | 0.619 |\n",
    "| VMD, fixed grid, alpha=2000 | 0.725 | 0.654 |\n",
    "| VMD, beat-aligned, alpha=2000 | 0.755 | 0.701 |\n",
    "| **VMD, beat-aligned, alpha=5** | **0.817** | **0.773** |\n",
    "| Chirplet, beat-aligned | 0.663 | 0.552 |\n",
    "\n",
    "The feature set never changed across those rows. The entire gain came from the\n",
    "evaluation split, the segmentation, and one hyperparameter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "863fccaa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d7d7adea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, math, time\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import scipy.io as sio\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "MAT_PATH = 'ECGData.mat'\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(MAT_PATH):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from google.colab import files; files.upload()\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f'Put {MAT_PATH} next to this notebook.')\n",
    "\n",
    "mat = sio.loadmat(MAT_PATH)\n",
    "ECGData = mat['ECGData']\n",
    "Data   = ECGData['Data'][0, 0]\n",
    "Labels = ECGData['Labels'][0, 0]\n",
    "label_list = np.array([str(Labels[i][0][0]) for i in range(len(Labels))])\n",
    "\n",
    "FS = 128\n",
    "print('Data:', Data.shape, '| %.0f s/record' % (Data.shape[1] / FS))\n",
    "print('Classes:', dict(zip(*np.unique(label_list, return_counts=True))))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4277f9b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Variational Mode Decomposition\n",
    "\n",
    "VMD splits a signal into `K` band-limited modes $u_k$, each compact around its own\n",
    "centre frequency $\\omega_k$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\min_{\\{u_k\\},\\{\\omega_k\\}} \\sum_k \\Big\\| \\partial_t\\big[(\\delta(t) + \\tfrac{j}{\\pi t}) * u_k(t)\\big]e^{-j\\omega_k t} \\Big\\|_2^2\n",
    "\\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\sum_k u_k = x$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Each mode is converted to its analytic signal, shifted to baseband, and its squared\n",
    "$H^1$ norm — its bandwidth — penalised by `alpha`. ADMM gives closed-form updates: a\n",
    "Wiener filter centred on $\\omega_k$ for the mode, and the centre of mass of\n",
    "$|\\hat u_k|^2$ for the frequency. Unlike EMD there is no recursive sifting — all modes\n",
    "are solved concurrently, which is what makes VMD robust to mode mixing.\n",
    "\n",
    "Implemented inline (no dependencies); verified against `vmdpy` to floating-point precision."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a9537187",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def vmd(signal, alpha=2000.0, tau=0.0, K=5, DC=False, tol=1e-7, max_iter=500):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Variational Mode Decomposition (Dragomiretskiy & Zosso, 2014).\n",
    "\n",
    "    alpha : bandwidth penalty. Large -> narrow modes. See section 5 -- the\n",
    "            conventional default of ~2000 is badly wrong for this data.\n",
    "    tau   : dual ascent step. 0.0 relaxes exact reconstruction so the\n",
    "            decomposition can shed broadband noise instead of forcing it\n",
    "            into a mode.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns u (K, N) sorted by centre frequency, omega (K,) in normalised\n",
    "    units (multiply by fs for Hz).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(signal, dtype=float).ravel()\n",
    "    N0 = x.size\n",
    "\n",
    "    half = N0 // 2                      # mirror-extend to soften boundary effects\n",
    "    f = np.concatenate([x[:half][::-1], x, x[N0 - half:][::-1]])\n",
    "    N = f.size\n",
    "    T = 1.0 / N\n",
    "\n",
    "    freqs = np.arange(1, N + 1) * T - 0.5 - T\n",
    "    f_hat_plus = np.fft.fftshift(np.fft.fft(f))\n",
    "    f_hat_plus[:N // 2] = 0             # analytic signal\n",
    "\n",
    "    omega = (0.5 / K) * np.arange(K)\n",
    "    if DC:\n",
    "        omega[0] = 0.0\n",
    "    u_hat = np.zeros((K, N), dtype=complex)\n",
    "    lam   = np.zeros(N, dtype=complex)\n",
    "    uDiff, n = tol + 1.0, 0\n",
    "\n",
    "    while uDiff > tol and n < max_iter:\n",
    "        u_hat_old = u_hat.copy()\n",
    "        for k in range(K):\n",
    "            resid = u_hat.sum(axis=0) - u_hat[k]\n",
    "            u_hat[k] = (f_hat_plus - resid - lam / 2.0) / \\\n",
    "                       (1.0 + alpha * (freqs - omega[k]) ** 2)\n",
    "            u_hat[k, :N // 2] = 0\n",
    "            if not (DC and k == 0):\n",
    "                pw = np.abs(u_hat[k, N // 2:]) ** 2\n",
    "                if pw.sum() > 0:\n",
    "                    omega[k] = (freqs[N // 2:] * pw).sum() / pw.sum()\n",
    "        lam = lam + tau * (u_hat.sum(axis=0) - f_hat_plus)\n",
    "        num = float(np.sum(np.abs(u_hat - u_hat_old) ** 2))\n",
    "        den = float(np.sum(np.abs(u_hat_old) ** 2))\n",
    "        uDiff = num / den if den > 1e-16 else tol + 1.0\n",
    "        n += 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    order = np.argsort(omega)\n",
    "    omega, u_hat = omega[order], u_hat[order]\n",
    "\n",
    "    full = np.zeros((K, N), dtype=complex)      # rebuild by Hermitian symmetry\n",
    "    full[:, N // 2:] = u_hat[:, N // 2:]\n",
    "    full[:, 1:N // 2 + 1] = np.conj(u_hat[:, N:N // 2 - 1:-1])\n",
    "    full[:, 0] = np.conj(full[:, -1])\n",
    "\n",
    "    u = np.real(np.fft.ifft(np.fft.ifftshift(full, axes=1), axis=1))\n",
    "    return u[:, half:half + N0], omega"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7e234437",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "_t = np.arange(500) / FS\n",
    "_x = (np.cos(2*np.pi*3*_t) + 0.6*np.cos(2*np.pi*12*_t) + 0.3*np.cos(2*np.pi*30*_t)\n",
    "      + 0.05*np.random.default_rng(0).standard_normal(500))\n",
    "_u, _om = vmd(_x, alpha=2000, tau=0.0, K=3)\n",
    "print('recovered:', np.round(_om * FS, 2), '| expected: [3 12 30]')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b7a1fd32",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Segmentation — fixed grid vs beat-aligned\n",
    "\n",
    "Two segmentations are built over the same records so they can be compared directly:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Fixed grid**: consecutive non-overlapping windows. QRS complexes land at arbitrary phase.\n",
    "- **Beat-aligned**: windows of *identical length* centred on a detected R peak.\n",
    "\n",
    "Same length, same records, same features — alignment is the only variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "`seg_record` is carried alongside because it is the group key for the split. Every\n",
    "segment from one record shares a label *and* a patient; a random split lets the model\n",
    "win by recognising the patient instead of the pathology (quantified in section 6)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "adbba657",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.signal import butter, filtfilt, find_peaks\n",
    "\n",
    "def detect_r_peaks(sig, fs=FS):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pan-Tompkins style: bandpass -> derivative -> square -> integrate -> peaks.\"\"\"\n",
    "    ny = fs / 2\n",
    "    b, a = butter(2, [5 / ny, min(20 / ny, 0.99)], btype='band')\n",
    "    x = filtfilt(b, a, sig)\n",
    "    sq = np.diff(x, prepend=x[0]) ** 2\n",
    "    w = int(0.15 * fs) | 1\n",
    "    integ = np.convolve(sq, np.ones(w) / w, mode='same')\n",
    "    peaks, _ = find_peaks(integ, height=integ.mean() + 0.5 * integ.std(),\n",
    "                          distance=int(0.25 * fs))\n",
    "    r = int(0.05 * fs)                          # snap to local extremum\n",
    "    return np.unique([max(0, p - r) + int(np.argmax(np.abs(x[max(0, p-r):p+r+1])))\n",
    "                      for p in peaks])\n",
    "\n",
    "# sanity: heart rates should be physiological\n",
    "for cls in ['ARR', 'CHF', 'NSR']:\n",
    "    hr = []\n",
    "    for i in np.where(label_list == cls)[0][:12]:\n",
    "        rr = np.diff(detect_r_peaks(Data[i])) / FS\n",
    "        rr = rr[(rr > 0.3) & (rr < 2.0)]\n",
    "        hr.append(60 / np.median(rr))\n",
    "    print(f'{cls}: median HR {np.mean(hr):5.1f} bpm')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f64d15b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ARR ~69 bpm, CHF ~92, NSR ~91. The elevated CHF rate is clinically consistent\n",
    "(tachycardia in heart failure), which is a reasonable sign the detector is working."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "08fa19cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SEG_LEN = 500                 # 3.9 s @ 128 Hz\n",
    "N_PER_REC = 25\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n",
    "half = SEG_LEN // 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Sfix, Sbeat, y, groups = [], [], [], []\n",
    "for i in range(Data.shape[0]):\n",
    "    sig = Data[i]\n",
    "    idx = rng.choice(len(sig) // SEG_LEN, N_PER_REC, replace=False)\n",
    "    pk = detect_r_peaks(sig)\n",
    "    pk = pk[(pk > half) & (pk < len(sig) - half)]\n",
    "    if len(pk) < N_PER_REC:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    bsel = rng.choice(len(pk), N_PER_REC, replace=False)\n",
    "    for j, b in zip(idx, bsel):\n",
    "        Sfix.append(sig[j * SEG_LEN:(j + 1) * SEG_LEN])\n",
    "        Sbeat.append(sig[pk[b] - half:pk[b] + half])\n",
    "        y.append(label_list[i]); groups.append(i)\n",
    "\n",
    "Sfix, Sbeat = np.asarray(Sfix), np.asarray(Sbeat)\n",
    "y, groups = np.asarray(y), np.asarray(groups)\n",
    "classes = np.unique(y)\n",
    "print('paired segments:', Sfix.shape, '| records:', len(np.unique(groups)))\n",
    "print(dict(zip(*np.unique(y, return_counts=True))))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "db41c4a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "t = np.arange(SEG_LEN) / FS\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(classes), 2, figsize=(13, 6), sharex=True)\n",
    "for r, cls in enumerate(classes):\n",
    "    i = np.where(y == cls)[0][0]\n",
    "    axes[r, 0].plot(t, Sfix[i], lw=.8);  axes[r, 0].set_ylabel(cls)\n",
    "    axes[r, 1].plot(t, Sbeat[i], lw=.8, color='tab:orange')\n",
    "    axes[r, 1].axvline(t[half], ls='--', c='k', lw=.8)\n",
    "    for c in range(2): axes[r, c].grid(alpha=.3)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title('fixed grid'); axes[0, 1].set_title('beat-aligned (R at dashed line)')\n",
    "for c in range(2): axes[-1, c].set_xlabel('time (s)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
