  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "656ed842",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Mode structure"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4de101bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "K_DEMO = 5\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(K_DEMO + 1, len(classes), figsize=(15, 11), sharex=True)\n",
    "for c, cls in enumerate(classes):\n",
    "    seg = Sbeat[np.where(y == cls)[0][0]]\n",
    "    seg = (seg - seg.mean()) / seg.std()\n",
    "    modes, om = vmd(seg, alpha=5.0, tau=0.0, K=K_DEMO)\n",
    "    axes[0, c].plot(t, seg, lw=.7, color='k')\n",
    "    axes[0, c].set_title(f'{cls} — original', fontsize=10)\n",
    "    for k in range(K_DEMO):\n",
    "        axes[k + 1, c].plot(t, modes[k], lw=.7)\n",
    "        axes[k + 1, c].set_title(f'mode {k}  ({om[k]*FS:.1f} Hz)', fontsize=9)\n",
    "for ax in axes.ravel(): ax.grid(alpha=.25); ax.tick_params(labelsize=7)\n",
    "for ax in axes[-1]: ax.set_xlabel('time (s)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b927b10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Modes stack low to high: baseline wander, then the QRS band, then the high-frequency\n",
    "noise floor. That ordering is what makes the per-mode features interpretable —\n",
    "`energy_ratio_m0` means \"how much baseline wander,\" not an arbitrary index."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "06569d5c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Features\n",
    "\n",
    "13 descriptors per mode plus 2 global -> `13K + 2 = 67` at K=5.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Group | Features |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Energy | energy, energy ratio |\n",
    "| Spectral | VMD centre frequency, spectral bandwidth |\n",
    "| Shape | std, kurtosis, skewness |\n",
    "| Complexity | Hjorth mobility, Hjorth complexity, permutation entropy |\n",
    "| Envelope | Hilbert envelope mean, std |\n",
    "| Relational | correlation with the original segment |\n",
    "| Global | entropy of the mode-energy distribution, reconstruction error |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1c998e42",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.signal import hilbert\n",
    "from scipy.stats import kurtosis, skew\n",
    "\n",
    "K = 5\n",
    "_FR = np.fft.rfftfreq(SEG_LEN, 1 / FS)\n",
    "\n",
    "def permutation_entropy(x, order=3):\n",
    "    n = len(x) - order + 1\n",
    "    emb = np.empty((n, order))\n",
    "    for i in range(order):\n",
    "        emb[:, i] = x[i:i + n]\n",
    "    code_ = (np.argsort(emb, axis=1) * (order ** np.arange(order))).sum(1)\n",
    "    c = np.bincount(code_); p = c[c > 0] / n\n",
    "    return -np.sum(p * np.log2(p)) / np.log2(math.factorial(order))\n",
    "\n",
    "def hjorth(x):\n",
    "    d1, d2 = np.diff(x), np.diff(x, 2)\n",
    "    v0, v1, v2 = x.var() + 1e-12, d1.var() + 1e-12, d2.var() + 1e-12\n",
    "    m = np.sqrt(v1 / v0)\n",
    "    return m, np.sqrt(v2 / v1) / m\n",
    "\n",
    "_PER_MODE = ['energy','energy_ratio','centre_hz','bandwidth_hz','std','kurtosis','skew',\n",
    "             'hjorth_mob','hjorth_comp','env_mean','env_std','perm_ent','corr_raw']\n",
    "FEATURE_NAMES = [f'{n}_m{k}' for k in range(K) for n in _PER_MODE] + \\\n",
    "                ['mode_energy_entropy', 'recon_err']\n",
    "\n",
    "def vmd_features(sig, K=K, alpha=5.0):\n",
    "    s = (sig - sig.mean()) / (sig.std() + 1e-12)   # morphology, not recording gain\n",
    "    u, om = vmd(s, alpha=alpha, tau=0.0, K=K, max_iter=500)\n",
    "    E = np.sum(u ** 2, axis=1); Et = E.sum() + 1e-12\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for k in range(K):\n",
    "        m = u[k]\n",
    "        env = np.abs(hilbert(m))\n",
    "        Pn = np.abs(np.fft.rfft(m)) ** 2\n",
    "        Pn = Pn / (Pn.sum() + 1e-12)\n",
    "        cf = float((_FR * Pn).sum())\n",
    "        bw = float(np.sqrt((((_FR - cf) ** 2) * Pn).sum()))\n",
    "        mob, comp = hjorth(m)\n",
    "        out += [E[k], E[k]/Et, om[k]*FS, bw, m.std(), kurtosis(m), skew(m),\n",
    "                mob, comp, env.mean(), env.std(), permutation_entropy(m),\n",
    "                float(np.corrcoef(m, s)[0, 1])]\n",
    "    p = E / Et\n",
    "    out += [-np.sum(p * np.log2(p + 1e-12)),\n",
    "            float(np.linalg.norm(s - u.sum(0)) / np.linalg.norm(s))]\n",
    "    return np.array(out, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(len(FEATURE_NAMES), 'features')\n",
    "_t0 = time.time(); vmd_features(Sbeat[0]); print('%.0f ms/segment' % ((time.time()-_t0)*1000))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e3d551c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Choosing alpha — the single largest effect in this notebook\n",
    "\n",
    "`alpha=2000` is the value carried around in most VMD tutorials. On this data it is\n",
    "**wrong by roughly two orders of magnitude**, and it costs more accuracy than every\n",
    "other choice here combined.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two failure modes squeeze from opposite ends:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **alpha too high** -> modes are narrow, the residual $x - \\sum_k u_k$ grows, and\n",
    "  discriminative energy is thrown away. At alpha=2000, **21% of signal energy** never\n",
    "  reaches the features.\n",
    "- **alpha too low** -> modes are wide, inter-mode correlation rises, and modes begin\n",
    "  duplicating each other's content.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that the centre-frequency-gap diagnostic normally used for choosing `K` does *not*\n",
    "catch the high-alpha failure — the gaps look fine at alpha=2000. **Residual energy is\n",
    "the diagnostic that matters here.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4fcf525b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "probe = Sbeat[np.random.default_rng(0).choice(len(Sbeat), 40, replace=False)]\n",
    "probe = (probe - probe.mean(1, keepdims=True)) / (probe.std(1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'alpha':>6} | {'min gap (Hz)':>12} | {'recon err':>9} | {'inter-mode corr':>15}\")\n",
    "diag = []\n",
    "for a in [1, 2, 5, 10, 50, 200, 2000, 8000]:\n",
    "    gaps, errs, ov = [], [], []\n",
    "    for s in probe:\n",
    "        u, om = vmd(s, alpha=a, tau=0.0, K=K, max_iter=500)\n",
    "        gaps.append(np.min(np.diff(om * FS)))\n",
    "        errs.append(np.linalg.norm(s - u.sum(0)) / np.linalg.norm(s))\n",
    "        Cc = np.corrcoef(u); ov.append(np.abs(Cc[np.triu_indices(K, 1)]).mean())\n",
    "    diag.append((a, np.mean(gaps), np.mean(errs), np.mean(ov)))\n",
    "    print(f'{a:6d} | {np.mean(gaps):12.2f} | {np.mean(errs):9.3f} | {np.mean(ov):15.3f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "diag = np.array(diag)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ax.semilogx(diag[:, 0], diag[:, 2], 'o-', label='reconstruction error')\n",
    "ax.semilogx(diag[:, 0], diag[:, 3], 's-', label='mean |inter-mode corr|')\n",
    "ax.axvline(5, ls='--', c='k', lw=1); ax.text(5.5, .3, 'alpha=5', fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('alpha'); ax.legend(); ax.grid(alpha=.3)\n",
    "ax.set_title('both failure modes are small only in a narrow window')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a03139cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The measured sweep (10 beats/record, subject-held-out) — the optimum is at **alpha ~ 5**:\n",
    "\n",
    "| alpha | 2 | 3 | **5** | 7 | 10 | 50 | 200 | 2000 | 8000 |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Accuracy | .804 | .811 | **.817** | .797 | .795 | .777 | .770 | .757 | .730 |\n",
    "| Macro-F1 | .757 | .769 | **.773** | .756 | .751 | .734 | .722 | .706 | .667 |\n",
    "\n",
    "At alpha=5 the modes are still cleanly separated (4.94 Hz minimum gap — *better* than\n",
    "alpha=2000's 3.67 Hz) with 0.3% residual, so this is a genuine optimum rather than a\n",
    "degenerate decomposition scoring well by accident.\n",
    "\n",
    "Re-run the cell below to reproduce it (slow — a few minutes)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "831606a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_ALPHA_SWEEP = False        # set True to reproduce\n",
    "\n",
    "if RUN_ALPHA_SWEEP:\n",
    "    from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "    from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedGroupKFold, cross_val_predict\n",
    "    from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, f1_score\n",
    "    sel = np.array([i for i in range(len(Sbeat)) if i % N_PER_REC < 10])\n",
    "    cvA = StratifiedGroupKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=0)\n",
    "    for a in [2, 5, 10, 50, 200, 2000]:\n",
    "        Xa = np.asarray([vmd_features(s, alpha=float(a)) for s in Sbeat[sel]])\n",
    "        pa = cross_val_predict(RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=200, random_state=0,\n",
    "                                                      n_jobs=-1),\n",
    "                               Xa, y[sel], groups=groups[sel], cv=cvA)\n",
    "        print(f'alpha={a:6d}  acc={accuracy_score(y[sel],pa):.4f} '\n",
    "              f'macroF1={f1_score(y[sel],pa,average=\"macro\"):.4f}', flush=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd3649be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Extract features for the 2x2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "18a46fc5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    from joblib import Parallel, delayed\n",
    "    _par = lambda S, a: np.asarray(Parallel(n_jobs=-1, verbose=1)(\n",
    "        delayed(vmd_features)(s, alpha=a) for s in S))\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    _par = lambda S, a: np.asarray([vmd_features(s, alpha=a) for s in S])\n",
    "\n",
    "FEATS = {}\n",
    "for tag, S, a in [('fix_a2000', Sfix, 2000.0), ('fix_a5', Sfix, 5.0),\n",
    "                  ('beat_a2000', Sbeat, 2000.0), ('beat_a5', Sbeat, 5.0)]:\n",
    "    c = f'X_{tag}.npy'\n",
    "    FEATS[tag] = np.load(c) if os.path.exists(c) else _par(S, a)\n",
    "    if not os.path.exists(c):\n",
    "        np.save(c, FEATS[tag])\n",
    "    print(tag, FEATS[tag].shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "af1c5db8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. The split, and why it dominates everything\n",
    "\n",
    "Every segment from record *i* carries the same label and the same patient. A random\n",
    "split scatters them across train and test, so the model can score well by memorising\n",
    "electrode placement, baseline wander signature, or resting heart rate — none of which\n",
    "is the pathology."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3041b8e8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import (StratifiedKFold, StratifiedGroupKFold,\n",
    "                                     cross_val_predict)\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, f1_score, classification_report,\n",
    "                             confusion_matrix)\n",
    "\n",
    "mk = lambda **kw: RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=200, random_state=0, n_jobs=-1, **kw)\n",
    "cv = StratifiedGroupKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=0)\n",
    "Xb = FEATS['beat_a5']\n",
    "\n",
    "p_rand = cross_val_predict(mk(), Xb, y, cv=StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=0))\n",
    "p_grp  = cross_val_predict(mk(), Xb, y, groups=groups, cv=cv)\n",
    "print('random  split (LEAKY) : acc=%.4f  macro-F1=%.4f'\n",
    "      % (accuracy_score(y, p_rand), f1_score(y, p_rand, average='macro')))\n",
    "print('grouped split (HONEST): acc=%.4f  macro-F1=%.4f'\n",
    "      % (accuracy_score(y, p_grp),  f1_score(y, p_grp,  average='macro')))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fec3aaa7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Expect a gap of roughly 15–20 points from leakage alone. Published accuracies on this\n",
    "dataset in the high 90s are almost always the leaky number."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1922b9ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Alignment x alpha — and they are not additive"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e2305805",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "R = {}\n",
    "for tag in ['fix_a2000', 'fix_a5', 'beat_a2000', 'beat_a5']:\n",
    "    p = cross_val_predict(mk(), FEATS[tag], y, groups=groups, cv=cv)\n",
    "    R[tag] = (accuracy_score(y, p), f1_score(y, p, average='macro'))\n",
    "    print(f'{tag:12s} acc={R[tag][0]:.4f}  macroF1={R[tag][1]:.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('alignment gain @alpha=2000: %+.4f acc' % (R['beat_a2000'][0] - R['fix_a2000'][0]))\n",
    "print('alignment gain @alpha=5   : %+.4f acc' % (R['beat_a5'][0]   - R['fix_a5'][0]))\n",
    "print('alpha gain @fixed grid    : %+.4f acc' % (R['fix_a5'][0]    - R['fix_a2000'][0]))\n",
    "print('alpha gain @beat-aligned  : %+.4f acc' % (R['beat_a5'][0]   - R['beat_a2000'][0]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc02b2a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "|  | alpha=2000 | alpha=5 |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **fixed grid** | 0.725 | 0.804 |\n",
    "| **beat-aligned** | 0.755 | **0.817** |\n",
    "\n",
    "The two effects are **sub-additive**. Beat alignment is worth +0.030 accuracy at\n",
    "alpha=2000 but only +0.013 once alpha is corrected.\n",
    "\n",
    "A plausible reading: at alpha=2000 the large residual absorbs the variance created by\n",
    "arbitrary QRS phase, so alignment helps by reducing what gets discarded. Once alpha=5\n",
    "retains ~99.7% of the signal, the features are already fairly phase-robust and there is\n",
    "less left for alignment to fix.\n",
    "\n",
    "This reverses the ranking — **alpha matters 2–5x more than alignment**, not the other\n",
    "way round."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4ac805a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(classification_report(y, p_grp, digits=3))\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y, p_grp, labels=classes)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 4))\n",
    "ax.imshow(cm, cmap='Blues')\n",
    "ax.set_xticks(range(len(classes)), classes); ax.set_yticks(range(len(classes)), classes)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('predicted'); ax.set_ylabel('true'); ax.set_title('beat-aligned, alpha=5')\n",
    "for i in range(len(classes)):\n",
    "    for j in range(len(classes)):\n",
    "        ax.text(j, i, cm[i, j], ha='center', va='center', fontsize=9,\n",
    "                color='white' if cm[i, j] > cm.max()/2 else 'black')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e757f83b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "CHF remains the hard class — precision 0.83 but recall 0.57, almost all of the loss\n",
    "going to ARR. Clinically unsurprising: heart failure patients frequently have\n",
    "arrhythmias, and with only 30 CHF records there are few independent subjects to\n",
    "generalise from."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a63fe962",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Class weighting does not help"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ed24373f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for w in [None, 'balanced']:\n",
    "    p = cross_val_predict(mk(class_weight=w), Xb, y, groups=groups, cv=cv)\n",
    "    print(f'class_weight={str(w):9s} acc={accuracy_score(y,p):.4f} '\n",
    "          f'macroF1={f1_score(y,p,average=\"macro\"):.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eb788bab",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`class_weight='balanced'` is the obvious lever for a 96/30/36 record imbalance, and it\n",
    "**hurts** — on both metrics, in both segmentations. Trading ARR recall for CHF recall\n",
    "is a bad deal when CHF has only 30 subjects: the extra CHF predictions are mostly wrong.\n",
    "The imbalance is at the *record* level, and no segment-level reweighting can manufacture\n",
    "subjects that aren't there."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "84f42a74",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Is the decomposition earning its cost?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "202f2e4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def baseline_features(sig):\n",
    "    # same descriptor families on the raw segment - no decomposition\n",
    "    z = (sig - sig.mean()) / (sig.std() + 1e-12)\n",
    "    Pn = np.abs(np.fft.rfft(z)) ** 2\n",
    "    Pn = Pn / (Pn.sum() + 1e-12)\n",
    "    cf = float((_FR * Pn).sum())\n",
    "    bw = float(np.sqrt((((_FR - cf) ** 2) * Pn).sum()))\n",
    "    mob, comp = hjorth(z)\n",
    "    bands = [Pn[(_FR >= a) & (_FR < b)].sum()\n",
    "             for a, b in [(0,2),(2,5),(5,10),(10,20),(20,40),(40,64)]]\n",
    "    return np.array([z.std(), kurtosis(z), skew(z), mob, comp, cf, bw,\n",
    "                     -np.sum(Pn*np.log2(Pn+1e-12))] + bands, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "B = np.asarray([baseline_features(s) for s in Sbeat])\n",
    "for nm, F in [('baseline (no VMD)', B), ('VMD alpha=5', Xb), ('both', np.hstack([Xb, B]))]:\n",
    "    p = cross_val_predict(mk(), F, y, groups=groups, cv=cv)\n",
    "    print('%-20s dim=%3d acc=%.4f macroF1=%.4f'\n",
    "          % (nm, F.shape[1], accuracy_score(y, p), f1_score(y, p, average='macro')))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2da053c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Chirplet transform — a tested alternative, and a negative result\n",
    "\n",
    "A chirplet atom generalises the Gabor atom with a **chirp rate** $c$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$g_{t_c,\\omega_c,c,\\Delta t}(t) \\propto e^{-\\frac{(t-t_c)^2}{2\\Delta t^2}}\n",
    "e^{j[\\omega_c(t-t_c) + \\frac{c}{2}(t-t_c)^2]}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Setting $c=0$ recovers Gabor/STFT. Adaptive chirplet decomposition greedily fits\n",
    "`P` atoms by matching pursuit and uses the **atom parameters themselves** as features —\n",
    "a sparse, physically interpretable code where the chirp rate directly encodes frequency\n",
    "sweep.\n",
    "\n",
    "The motivating hypothesis was that if *where the QRS band sits* is discriminative under\n",
    "VMD, then *how that frequency moves* should be too. It did not hold up."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6052bec4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TC_STEP = 20\n",
    "DT_GRID = np.array([8., 16., 32., 64.])                                  # samples\n",
    "CR_GRID = np.array([-200., -100., -50., -20., 0., 20., 50., 100., 200.]) # Hz/s\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_kernels(N, fs=FS):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Modulation kernels, signal-independent. Stacked into one (M, N) matrix:\n",
    "    frequency is NOT gridded, since for fixed (tc, dt, c) the inner product\n",
    "    against every omega_c is a single batched FFT.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    params, rows = [], []\n",
    "    for tc in np.arange(0, N, TC_STEP, dtype=float):\n",
    "        tt = np.arange(N) - tc; t2 = tt ** 2\n",
    "        for dt in DT_GRID:\n",
    "            env = np.exp(-t2 / (2 * dt ** 2)); nrm = np.linalg.norm(env)\n",
    "            if nrm < 1e-6: continue\n",
    "            for cr in CR_GRID:\n",
    "                c = 2 * np.pi * cr / (fs ** 2)          # Hz/s -> rad/sample^2\n",
    "                params.append((tc, dt, cr))\n",
    "                rows.append(env * np.exp(1j * 0.5 * c * t2) / nrm)\n",
    "    return np.asarray(params), np.conj(np.asarray(rows))\n",
    "\n",
    "def chirplet_mp(signal, P=8, fs=FS, kernels=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Matching pursuit on the analytic signal (so atoms aren't wasted on\n",
    "    conjugate pairs). Returns P atom-parameter dicts.\"\"\"\n",
    "    x = np.asarray(signal, float); N = x.size\n",
    "    r = hilbert(x).astype(complex)\n",
    "    E0 = float(np.sum(np.abs(r) ** 2)) + 1e-12\n",
    "    params, Kc = kernels if kernels is not None else build_kernels(N, fs)\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for _ in range(P):\n",
    "        S = np.abs(np.fft.fft(Kc * r[None, :], axis=1))\n",
    "        S[:, N // 2:] = 0                               # positive frequencies only\n",
    "        row, k = divmod(int(np.argmax(S)), N)\n",
    "        tc, dt, cr = params[row]\n",
    "        tt = np.arange(N) - tc\n",
    "        c = 2 * np.pi * cr / (fs ** 2)\n",
    "        g = np.exp(-tt**2 / (2*dt**2)) * np.exp(1j * (0.5*c*tt**2 + 2*np.pi*k/N*tt))\n",
    "        g /= (np.linalg.norm(g) + 1e-12)\n",
    "        a = np.vdot(g, r); r = r - a * g\n",
    "        out.append(dict(tc=tc/fs, fc=k*fs/N, cr=cr, dt=dt/fs, amp=float(np.abs(a)),\n",
    "                        res=float(np.sum(np.abs(r)**2) / E0)))\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "# validation: a 15 Hz/s sweep, and a pure tone\n",
    "_ker = build_kernels(SEG_LEN)\n",
    "_tt = np.arange(SEG_LEN) / FS\n",
    "_ch = np.exp(-((_tt-2.0)**2)/(2*0.35**2)) * np.cos(2*np.pi*(8*_tt + 0.5*15*_tt**2))\n",
    "_to = np.exp(-((_tt-2.0)**2)/(2*0.35**2)) * np.cos(2*np.pi*20*_tt)\n",
    "print('chirp atom0:', {k: round(v,2) for k,v in chirplet_mp(_ch,1,kernels=_ker)[0].items()})\n",
    "print('tone  atom0:', {k: round(v,2) for k,v in chirplet_mp(_to,1,kernels=_ker)[0].items()})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3e568bfe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Validation passes: the sweep returns 20 Hz/s (nearest grid point to the true 15) at the\n",
    "right time centre; the pure tone returns exactly 0 Hz/s and captures ~94% of the energy\n",
    "in a single atom."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7c33387b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "P_ATOMS = 8\n",
    "CHIRP_NAMES = [f'{n}_a{p}' for p in range(P_ATOMS)\n",
    "               for n in ['tc','fc','chirprate','abs_chirprate','dt','amp','resid']] + \\\n",
    "              ['fc_spread','mean_abs_chirprate','frac_chirped','first_atom_share',\n",
    "               'final_resid','amp_entropy']\n",
    "\n",
    "def chirplet_features(sig, P=P_ATOMS, kernels=None):\n",
    "    s = (sig - sig.mean()) / (sig.std() + 1e-12)\n",
    "    at = chirplet_mp(s, P=P, kernels=kernels)\n",
    "    f = []\n",
    "    for a in at:\n",
    "        f += [a['tc'], a['fc'], a['cr'], abs(a['cr']), a['dt'], a['amp'], a['res']]\n",
    "    fcs = np.array([a['fc'] for a in at]); crs = np.array([a['cr'] for a in at])\n",
    "    am  = np.array([a['amp'] for a in at]); pp = am / (am.sum() + 1e-12)\n",
    "    f += [float(fcs.std()), float(np.abs(crs).mean()), float((crs != 0).mean()),\n",
    "          float(am[0]/(am.sum()+1e-12)), at[-1]['res'],\n",
    "          float(-np.sum(pp*np.log2(pp+1e-12)))]\n",
    "    return np.array(f, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "\n",
    "_c = 'X_chirp_beat.npy'\n",
    "if os.path.exists(_c):\n",
    "    Xc = np.load(_c)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    Xc = np.asarray([chirplet_features(s, kernels=_ker) for s in Sbeat]); np.save(_c, Xc)\n",
    "Xc = np.nan_to_num(Xc)\n",
    "\n",
    "for nm, F in [('VMD alpha=5', Xb), ('Chirplet', Xc), ('VMD + Chirplet', np.hstack([Xb, Xc]))]:\n",
    "    p = cross_val_predict(mk(), F, y, groups=groups, cv=cv)\n",
    "    print('%-16s dim=%3d acc=%.4f macroF1=%.4f'\n",
    "          % (nm, F.shape[1], accuracy_score(y, p), f1_score(y, p, average='macro')))\n",
    "\n",
    "rfc = mk().fit(Xc, y)\n",
    "print('\\ntop chirplet features:')\n",
    "for i in np.argsort(rfc.feature_importances_)[::-1][:8]:\n",
    "    print(f'  {CHIRP_NAMES[i]:22s} {rfc.feature_importances_[i]:.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "40b56b8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Chirplet loses clearly (~0.66 vs 0.76 accuracy against VMD at the *same* alpha=2000-era\n",
    "settings, and further behind alpha=5), and concatenating the two is **worse than VMD\n",
    "alone** — feature dilution.\n",
    "\n",
    "The importances say why the hypothesis failed. The useful chirplet features are almost\n",
    "all **residual** terms (`resid_a7`, `final_resid`, `resid_a6`), i.e. *how compressible\n",
    "is this segment by chirplets* — a sparsity measure. The chirp rates themselves barely\n",
    "register. Frequency dynamics, at this resolution, are not where the class information lives.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Caveat on scope.** The dictionary is coarse — 9 chirp rates, $t_c$ every 20 samples,\n",
    "and 8 atoms across a 3.9 s window is ~1.6 atoms per beat. This is a fair test of *this\n",
    "configuration*, not a verdict on chirplet decomposition. A denser grid with P~30 could\n",
    "plausibly change the answer, at several times the cost."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "03f29588",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Which features carry the signal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b63d4471",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rf = mk().fit(Xb, y)\n",
    "o = np.argsort(rf.feature_importances_)[::-1][:20]\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "plt.barh(range(len(o)), rf.feature_importances_[o][::-1])\n",
    "plt.yticks(range(len(o)), [FEATURE_NAMES[i] for i in o][::-1], fontsize=8)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('impurity importance'); plt.title('Top 20 (beat-aligned, alpha=5)')\n",
    "plt.grid(alpha=.3, axis='x'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "70072740",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`perm_ent_m4` dominates — permutation entropy of the *highest*-frequency mode. At\n",
    "alpha=5 that mode sits near 43 Hz and retains real content rather than being a discarded\n",
    "noise band, which is exactly what the alpha correction changed. Kurtosis across the mid\n",
    "modes follows, picking up the impulsiveness of ectopic beats, and `recon_err` stays in\n",
    "the top five — how much of the segment resists band-limited decomposition is itself\n",
    "informative.\n",
    "\n",
    "Impurity importance is biased toward high-cardinality continuous features; confirm with\n",
    "`sklearn.inspection.permutation_importance` on a held-out fold before reporting these."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62c48a1e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. What this exercise actually showed\n",
    "\n",
    "**The feature set was never the bottleneck.** Accuracy moved 0.725 -> 0.817 and macro-F1\n",
    "0.654 -> 0.773 without adding a single feature. Both gains came from segmentation and one\n",
    "hyperparameter. Most of the initial effort went into feature engineering, which was the\n",
    "wrong place to spend it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Three predictions that turned out wrong**, recorded because the corrections are the\n",
    "useful part:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. *\"R-peak alignment is likely a bigger win than any VMD hyperparameter.\"* False —\n",
    "   alpha is worth 2–5x more, and the two are sub-additive.\n",
    "2. *\"`class_weight='balanced'` is the honest lever for the imbalance.\"* False — it hurts\n",
    "   on both metrics in both segmentations.\n",
    "3. *\"Chirplet is well-motivated rather than a shot in the dark.\"* False — it loses by ~10\n",
    "   points, dilutes the VMD features when concatenated, and the little it contributes comes\n",
    "   from residual/sparsity terms rather than chirp rates.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Open threads**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The alpha sweep used 10 beats/record; the optimum should be confirmed at full scale,\n",
    "  and alpha interacts with `K` (wider modes may want fewer of them) — the 2D sweep is unrun.\n",
    "- `tau` was fixed at 0 throughout. With alpha=5 the residual is already ~0.3%, so `tau`\n",
    "  has much less to do than it did at alpha=2000; worth confirming rather than assuming.\n",
    "- A denser chirplet dictionary with P~30 is the only fair way to close out that comparison.\n",
    "- Multi-lead data would test whether these features survive the transfer; single-lead\n",
    "  results on 162 subjects do not establish much about generalisation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cost note for a pretraining pipeline.** VMD is a few hundred ADMM iterations per\n",
    "segment and does not vectorise across a batch — batching was measurably *slower* here,\n",
    "since memory traffic dominates once the arrays leave cache. Precompute and cache; do not\n",
    "run VMD inside a dataloader."
   ]
  }
